#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:84
msgid ""
"The asymmetry between the populated and empty literals is the gotcha worth "
"calling out:"
msgstr ""
"Asimetrija između popunjenog i praznog literala zamka je koju vrijedi "
"istaknuti:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:87
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Braces with **items in them** -- ``{1, 2, 3}`` -- are a set literal; braces "
"with **key-value pairs** -- ``{\"a\": 1}`` -- are a dict literal. The parser"
" tells them apart by what is inside."
msgstr ""
"Vitičaste zagrade sa **stavkama u sebi** -- ``{1, 2, 3}`` -- literal su "
"skupa; vitičaste zagrade s **parovima ključ-vrijednost** -- ``{\"a\": 1}`` "
"-- literal su rječnika. Parser ih razlikuje prema onome što je unutra."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:91
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Braces with **nothing inside** -- ``{}`` -- are an empty dict, not an empty "
"set. Dicts came first; the empty literal belongs to them. An empty set has "
"no braces literal at all and must be written ``set()``."
msgstr ""
"Vitičaste zagrade s **ničim unutra** -- ``{}`` -- prazan su rječnik, a ne "
"prazan skup. Rječnici su došli prvi; prazan literal pripada njima. Prazan "
"skup uopće nema literal s vitičastim zagradama i mora se napisati kao "
"``set()``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:96
msgid ""
"A common pattern when only the keys of a dict are ever read is to switch to "
"a set -- it makes the intent obvious and trims the unused values out of "
"memory."
msgstr ""
"Uobičajen obrazac kada se uvijek čitaju samo ključevi rječnika jest prijelaz"
" na skup -- on čini namjeru očiglednom i uklanja neiskorištene vrijednosti "
"iz memorije."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:101
msgid "Adding and removing"
msgstr "Dodavanje i uklanjanje"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:103
msgid ":meth:`set.add` -- insert one item."
msgstr ":meth:`set.add` -- umeće jednu stavku."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:104
msgid ""
":meth:`set.discard` -- remove an item if it is present, do nothing if it is "
"not."
msgstr ""
":meth:`set.discard` -- uklanja stavku ako je prisutna, ne čini ništa ako "
"nije."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:106
msgid ""
":meth:`set.remove` -- remove an item; raise :exc:`KeyError` if it is "
"missing."
msgstr ""
":meth:`set.remove` -- uklanja stavku; izaziva :exc:`KeyError` ako je nema."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:108
msgid ":meth:`set.clear` -- empty the set."
msgstr ":meth:`set.clear` -- prazni skup."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:123
msgid "Membership"
msgstr "Pripadnost"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:125
msgid ""
"The ``in`` operator tests for membership. On a set it is roughly constant "
"time regardless of size -- which is the main reason to choose a set over a "
":class:`list` when you only need to ask \"is this value in there\":"
msgstr ""
"Operator ``in`` provjerava pripadnost. Na skupu je to otprilike konstantno "
"vrijeme bez obzira na veličinu -- što je glavni razlog da odaberete skup "
"umjesto :class:`list` kada samo trebate pitati \"je li ova vrijednost "
"unutra\":"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:135
msgid ""
"A :class:`list` with the same contents would scan from the start each time, "
"which is fine for ten items but slow for ten thousand."
msgstr ""
":class:`list` s istim sadržajem pretraživao bi se od početka svaki put, što "
"je u redu za deset stavki, ali sporo za deset tisuća."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:140
msgid "Set operations"
msgstr "Operacije nad skupovima"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:142
msgid ""
"Two sets can be combined with the usual mathematical operations. Each has "
"both an operator form and a method form:"
msgstr ""
"Dva skupa mogu se kombinirati uobičajenim matematičkim operacijama. Svaka "
"ima i oblik operatora i oblik metode:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:145
msgid "``a | b`` or ``a.union(b)`` -- everything in either set."
msgstr "``a | b`` ili ``a.union(b)`` -- sve što je u bilo kojem od skupova."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:146
msgid "``a & b`` or ``a.intersection(b)`` -- only what appears in both."
msgstr ""
"``a & b`` ili ``a.intersection(b)`` -- samo ono što se pojavljuje u oba."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:148
msgid "``a - b`` or ``a.difference(b)`` -- in ``a`` but not in ``b``."
msgstr "``a - b`` ili ``a.difference(b)`` -- u ``a``\\ , ali ne u ``b``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:149
msgid "``a ^ b`` or ``a.symmetric_difference(b)`` -- in one but not both."
msgstr ""
"``a ^ b`` ili ``a.symmetric_difference(b)`` -- u jednom, ali ne u oba."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:168
msgid ""
"The operator forms are read-only; the method forms accept any iterable on "
"the right, not just another set (``a.union([5, 6])``). Pick whichever reads "
"better in context."
msgstr ""
"Oblici operatora samo su za čitanje; oblici metoda prihvaćaju bilo koji "
"iterabilni objekt s desne strane, ne samo drugi skup (\\ ``a.union([5, "
"6])``\\ ). Odaberite onaj koji se bolje čita u kontekstu."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:173
msgid "What can go in a set"
msgstr "Što može ići u skup"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:175
msgid ""
"Set elements must be *hashable* -- the same constraint as :class:`dict` "
"keys. :class:`int`, :class:`float`, :class:`str`, :class:`bool`, "
":class:`bytes`, and :class:`tuple` (when its contents are themselves "
"hashable) all work. :class:`list` and :class:`dict` do not; trying to add "
"one raises :exc:`TypeError`."
msgstr ""
"Elementi skupa moraju biti *raspršivi* (hashable) -- isto ograničenje kao "
"kod ključeva :class:`dict`\\ . :class:`int`\\ , :class:`float`\\ , "
":class:`str`\\ , :class:`bool`\\ , :class:`bytes` i :class:`tuple` (kada je "
"njezin sadržaj sam po sebi raspršiv) svi rade. :class:`list` i :class:`dict`"
" ne rade; pokušaj dodavanja jednog od njih izaziva :exc:`TypeError`\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:183
msgid "frozenset"
msgstr "frozenset"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:185
msgid ""
"A regular :class:`set` is mutable: every call to ``add`` / ``remove`` / "
"``discard`` changes the object in place. That mutability disqualifies it "
"from being hashable, so a set *cannot* be used as a :class:`dict` key or as "
"a member of another set."
msgstr ""
"Obični :class:`set` je promjenjiv: svaki poziv ``add`` / ``remove`` / "
"``discard`` mijenja objekt na mjestu. Ta promjenjivost ga diskvalificira iz "
"toga da bude raspršiv, pa se skup *ne može* koristiti kao ključ "
":class:`dict` ni kao član drugog skupa."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:191
msgid ""
":class:`frozenset` is the immutable counterpart. It has the same lookups and"
" operators (``in``, ``|``, ``&``, ``-``, ``^``) as :class:`set`, but no "
"``add`` / ``remove`` and no methods that mutate. Because nothing can ever "
"change its contents, the hash of a :class:`frozenset` is well-defined -- so "
"it *is* hashable:"
msgstr ""
":class:`frozenset` nepromjenjiv je pandan. Ima iste pretrage i operatore (\\"
" ``in``\\ , ``|``\\ , ``&``\\ , ``-``\\ , ``^``\\ ) kao :class:`set`\\ , ali"
" nema ``add`` / ``remove`` ni metode koje ga mijenjaju. Budući da se njegov "
"sadržaj nikad ne može promijeniti, raspršena vrijednost (hash) za "
":class:`frozenset` dobro je definirana -- pa *jest* raspršiv:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:214
msgid ""
"Construct a frozenset from any iterable -- ``frozenset()`` for the empty "
"case, ``frozenset(some_set)`` to take an immutable snapshot of an existing "
"set:"
msgstr ""
"Frozenset se gradi iz bilo kojeg iterabilnog objekta -- ``frozenset()`` za "
"prazan slučaj, ``frozenset(some_set)`` za nepromjenjivu snimku postojećeg "
"skupa:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:223
msgid "Two common reasons to reach for it:"
msgstr "Dva česta razloga da posegnete za njim:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:225
msgid ""
"**Use as a dict key or set member.** Anywhere a single value cannot capture "
"what you need, a :class:`frozenset` of values can -- \"the set of features "
"supported by this driver\", \"the set of pins this profile uses\"."
msgstr ""
"**Uporaba kao ključa rječnika ili člana skupa.** Svugdje gdje jedna "
"vrijednost ne može obuhvatiti ono što vam treba, može :class:`frozenset` "
"vrijednosti -- \"skup značajki koje ovaj upravljač podržava\", \"skup pinova"
" koje ovaj profil koristi\"."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/python/collections/sets.rst:229
msgid ""
"**Lock down a constant.** A module-level :class:`frozenset` of allowed names"
" cannot be accidentally mutated by a caller; a regular :class:`set` can. "
"Prefer :class:`frozenset` for anything that is meant to be read-only after "
"construction."
msgstr ""
"**Zaključavanje konstante.** :class:`frozenset` na razini modula s "
"dopuštenim imenima ne može slučajno izmijeniti pozivatelj; obični "
":class:`set` može. Dajte prednost :class:`frozenset` za sve što treba biti "
"samo za čitanje nakon stvaranja."
